 "result": "`Config.from_prefixed_env()` in `src/tessel/config.py` (around lines 126–180) does this.\n\n- **Prefix:** the default prefix is `\"TESSEL\"`. It reads each `TESSEL_*` variable and strips the prefix, so `TESSEL_SECRET_KEY` becomes the key `SECRET_KEY`.\n- **Type conversion:** each value is passed through the `loads` parameter, which defaults to `json.loads`. That turns `\"true\"` into `True`, `\"5\"` into `5`, and `\"[1,2]\"` into a list. If parsing fails, the value stays a plain string.\n- **Nested keys:** a double underscore (`__`) marks nesting. `TESSEL_DB__HOST` becomes `config[\"DB\"][\"HOST\"]`, and any missing intermediate dicts are created.\n\nI only read the grep matches for this file, not the full method body, so the details above come from the docstring and key lines.",
